# 1.5 Carat Radiant Cut Diamond Ring: Lab Wins. Here's the Math

Buying a 1.5 carat radiant cut diamond ring means answering one question honestly: is the size jump from 1ct worth what you are about to pay? The honest answer depends entirely on whether you're buying lab or natural.

This guide covers every combination — lab and natural stones, 12 settings, every metal, and complete ring totals from certified market data. The 1.5ct Jump Rule and the Weight-to-Width Gap will give you the framework to make the right call.

Every price on this page is stone plus setting. Every table has a "What this means" column.

**TL;DR:**
- → **For lab buyers: yes** — 1.5ct lab ring from $2,370, versus $1,727 at 1ct. A real size upgrade for $643 more.
- → **For natural buyers: usually no** — 1.5ct natural ring starts at $8,564, versus $3,178 at 1ct. A 2.7× price jump for ~12% more face-up area.
- 1.5 carat radiant cut diamond rings from [$2,370 lab](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) or [$8,564 natural](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29651855?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- → Best lab: [1.5ct D-VVS1 IGI $1,772](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929649?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$2,632**
- → Best natural: [1.5ct G-VS2 GIA $7,704](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29651855?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$8,564**
- G-VS2 remains the grade floor at 1.5ct — below it, compromises show; above it, improvements are invisible to the naked eye

